## THE DECISIONS OF THIS COMMIT (each Tuesday's default as coordinator; each a Question at the stamp)
- **D1: step 5 only, out of step order (Q1, STOP-CLASS).** The commission's order is step 2 first; steps 2 to 4 are each a STOP of its own rule (no operation under `contracts/oxpd1/`), so the first pair this lane CAN build is step 5's. No pair is half-built: both of step 5's calls (the write and its undo) ship together.
- **D2: a new public class beside a read-only client.** `Oxpd1Writer` holds the writes; `Oxpd1Client` keeps its public surface (the two reads and `Dispose`), so the landed cell C04 (`ContractTests.cs:122`, `C04_no_row_and_no_public_method_writes_and_a_planted_write_is_found`) stays unchanged and green (MEASURED in the whole-solution run). The writer reaches the device only through the client's internal `SendWriteAsync`, which calls the client's one `SendAsync`: no second handler, no second pin check (B1996 F13: no further copy of the pin rule). `SendAsync` now takes the action text and an answer reader in place of the read's catalogue row (a private signature; the reads' bytes on the wire are unchanged: every landed read cell green).
- **D3: a dry run is the default and reads nothing.** `Oxpd1WriteCall.Execute` is `false` unless the caller sets it (`with { Execute = true }`); a dry run builds the envelope with the client's addressing version and returns it with the URL and the action, and calls neither the setting reader nor the network (W02 counts 0 setting reads and 0 requests).
- **D4: `Applied` is three-valued and the undo follows it.** `No` only where nothing could have taken effect: nothing sent (`NoCredential`, `PinRefused`) or the credentials refused (401, 403: HP's description of both operations, "Missing credentials will be challenged with a 401 response. Invalid credentials will result in a 403 response.", `authentication.wsdl`, DERIVED that the operation did not run; UNMEASURED on a device). `Yes` on the empty response element. `Unknown` on every other end. The undo is returned for `Yes` and `Unknown`; it is SAFE to send when the end is unknown because HP's description of `UnregisterAuthenticationAgent` says "If the agent ID does not match an existing OXPd authentication agent record's ID, this method will succeed (no exception thrown), but will have no effect." (DERIVED from the committed file; the stub does the same; UNMEASURED on a device). The register is idempotent by id ("If a record with the same ID already exists in the device's list, its content is replaced", the same file).
- **D5: the record the test registers** (Q4): the id (lower case), a name of 1 to 100 characters used also as its `en-US` display name and description, the agent service (`binding` `Soap12`) and the prompt page (`binding` `Plain`), each an absolute `https` address without user information of at most 256 characters, time-outs 5 and 5 seconds (1 to 300), the pre-prompt check off, the sign-out notification off (retries 0, interval 1), no `serverContextId`, **no `networkCredentials`** (the device calls the agent with none; a call-back credential is spike S2's, B1996 F12). Both request bodies validate against HP's committed schema (W01).
- **D6: no guard in the adapter** (Q2, STOP-CLASS): see BLUF 2. The README's Limits say the writer counts nothing across calls.
- **D7: the record line of the client reads `OXPd 1.x call` for reads and writes alike** (`Oxpd1Client.cs:293`; it read `OXPd 1.x read`; no landed cell reads that word, MEASURED by `git grep -n -i 'OXPd 1.x read'` over `tests` at BASE: no line) (Q6).
- **D8: ONE commit, on a new branch from BASE; the rebase rule before the first push only** (SHARED FILES AND MAIN).

## THE REQUIRED SECTION: what is the writer handed that is NOT the tested shape?
**The properties (each a behaviour sentence this lane freezes; the paths named are the only writers and callers, found by `grep -n` over the two `src` files at the fixed tree):** (P1) a call whose `Execute` is not set sends nothing and reads no setting (`Oxpd1Writer.WriteAsync`, the only caller of `SendWriteAsync`, returns at `:261` before it); (P2) an executed call sends at most ONE request and never retries (`WriteAsync` calls `SendWriteAsync` once; `SendWriteAsync` calls `SendAsync` once; `SendAsync` calls `_http.SendAsync` once, `Oxpd1Client.cs:141`); (P3) every end that may have applied a register carries its undo (`Oxpd1Writer.cs:270` to `:274`); (P4) `Applied` is `No` only where nothing could have taken effect; (P5) the admin password is in no result text and no record (`Oxpd1WriteResult.Request` is the envelope, which never holds it; the client's `Record` scrubs); (P6) every operation sent is an operation of the committed bindings (the write catalogue, `checks_w1.py` check 6). **At least these shapes; any other shape you meet: name it in STATUS with its cell or a named limit, never leave it out, and add no cell beyond the patch.** The commission's item 11 asks for three shapes NOT the tested shape per property, and for W1 by name: **a device that answers a write with a fault (H3), a device that times out AFTER the write may have applied (H4: is the undo then safe to send?), and a second write on the same run (H6, H7).**
| # | Shape | Cell, mutant or named limit |
|---|---|---|
| H1 | **no `Execute`: a register and an unregister** | W02: `DryRun` true, `Outcome` null, `Applied` `No`, `Undo` null, the URL path `/hp/device/webservices/OXPd/AuthenticationService`, the action ends with the operation, 0 requests at the stub, 0 agents, 0 setting reads; `mDryRunIgnored` |
| H2 | **a register executed, then its undo executed** | W03: each `Answered`, `Applied` `Yes`; the stub holds the id after the first and none after the second; the register's undo is the unregister of the same id with `Execute` false; exactly 2 requests, both `POST`, both carrying the password; `mUndoExecutes` |
| H3 | **a SOAP fault (500) on a register** (commission shape 1) | W04: `Fault`, code `s:Sender`, `Applied` `Unknown`, the undo given, 1 request, 0 agents; the undo then sent is `Answered` and leaves 0 agents (HP's no-effect success); `mUnknownIsYes`, `mUndoOnlyWhenYes`, `mResendOnFailure` |
| H4 | **a time-out AFTER the stub applied the register** (commission shape 2) | W05: the stub stores the id, then waits 3 s; `Timeout` 1 s; `TimedOut`, `Applied` `Unknown`, the stub HOLDS the id, the undo given; the undo sent removes it; the same undo sent again is `Answered` (no effect); 3 password-bearing requests in all. **Is the undo then safe to send? Yes on the stub, by HP's description (D4); UNMEASURED on a device.** `mUnknownIsYes`, `mUndoOnlyWhenYes`, `mResendOnFailure` |
| H5 | **a 403, a 401, a missing setting, a wrong pin** | W06 (4 cases): `Forbidden`, `Unauthorized`, `NoCredential`, `PinRefused`; `Applied` `No`; no undo; 0 agents; 1, 1, 0, 0 requests; `mRefusedUnknown`, `mPinUnknown`, `mResendOnFailure` |
| H6 | **a second write on the same run** (commission shape 3): the register, then its undo, on one client | W03: 2 requests, each ONE password-bearing request; nothing else sent |
| H7 | **a second write after a refused password (401, 403)** | NO CELL; a named limit (D6, Q2): the writer counts nothing across calls, so a second executed call sends again; the stop after one refusal is the caller's (L5's pattern, the next lane's lab wiring), the per-device count the shared device-trust component's (B1996 F16) |
| H8 | **an answer that is not the empty response element: a child inside it; the other operation's response** | W09 (2 cases): `MalformedAnswer`, `Applied` `Unknown`, the undo given, 1 request; `mEmptyAnswerLoose` (the `child` row), `mUnknownIsYes`, `mUndoOnlyWhenYes`, `mResendOnFailure` |
| H9 | **another status (a 307 among them), an oversized answer, a broken connection** | NO CELL; DERIVED: each is an end of the client's `SendAsync` (`HttpStatus`, `TooLarge`, `TransportFailed`; the landed read cells K06 and the size cells cover the client's side) and falls in the switch's default arm, `Unknown`, with the undo; the redirect is never followed (`AllowAutoRedirect = false`, `Oxpd1Client.cs:46`) |
| H10 | **the HTTP layer resending the write** (a pooled connection reused; a 401 challenge) | NO CELL; RELAYED: gate B2002 MEASURED exactly one password-bearing request over 18 shapes for the same client's reads (macOS); the write goes through the same `SendAsync` and handler (no `Credentials` set, so no challenge is answered); UNMEASURED for writes on any leg |
| H11 | **the caller's own cancellation while a write is in flight** | NO CELL; a named limit: it throws `OperationCanceledException` (the client's documented misuse path) and returns NO result, so no undo is handed back; the caller still holds the call and its `Undo` property |
| H12 | **a record: an empty id, a blank or 101-character name, an `http` address, user information, a 257-character address, a time-out of 0 or 301, an unregister of the empty id** | W07: each refused (`ArgumentException` or `ArgumentOutOfRangeException`); control: 100 characters, time-outs 1 and 300 taken; `mHttpTaken`, `mNameUnbounded` |
| H13 | **both request bodies against HP's committed schema; a binding value the schema does not list** | W01: both validate (`ContractTests.Validate`, the landed helper); the planted `Soap11` is refused; the two rows equal the committed binding's action, service, namespace and operation; `mWrongBinding` |
| H14 | **the password in a result's text or the record file** | W08: the two results' `ToString` and `Request` and every file of the record folder hold neither the password nor its Basic token; the record names both operations |
| H15 | **the password in a fault code; the password inside a name or address the caller gave** | NO CELL; a named limit: the fault code is scrubbed and cut by the same code as a read's (`Oxpd1Client.cs:213` onwards, the landed read cells K12 to K16 cover `Scrub`); a dry run reads no password, so its envelope is not scrubbed and holds whatever the caller put in the record (README Limits) |
| H16 | **an operation outside the committed bindings** | `checks_w1.py` check 6 (every quoted operation name in the added `src` lines is one of the 30 binding operations; control `RegisterUIButton` named); W01's row-against-binding check |
| H17 | **steps 2, 3 and 4** | NOT BUILT: their operations are in no committed file (Q1); the README's Limits say so |
| H18 | **the undo of an unregister; the end-of-session list of what is still registered** | NOT BUILT, named limits: an unregister's `Undo` is null (re-registering needs the record); "confirm all undone" (B1996 F19) is a later lab command |
| H19 | **a real device: its answer, its fault subcodes, whether it applies before it refuses, the endpoint path** | NEVER in this lane; a named limit: all UNMEASURED |
| H20 | **any shape you meet that is not above** | a named limit in STATUS (no new cell) |
